re":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"953e1aa93e99cb02e4b8e4cf771aa6523a56614a9979c61cb78c761ee6be676e","event_uuid":"c806a08b-a56b-450b-89d8-3136ddfb503d","position":{"commit_sha":"3ce234d7a902e7fb6a7dc0d4bad538199c228c4b","position":"1794515771281479001-c806a08b-a56b-450b-89d8-3136ddfb503d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"aa911de4b12e3eec214ca026aa529c106210a1f8c6e4f28a31b5fb8731e3246f","event_uuid":"da8bef3f-47fc-4d89-87ca-2db3f0a29a0d","position":{"commit_sha":"48c0dc7627f67cf4310390c16fb423c34c16a850","position":"1794515786718482001-da8bef3f-47fc-4d89-87ca-2db3f0a29a0d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"62e66fcdd74da11624ba9b7af7dbca78355ca498b0d7ddc7959022eb43f833ef","event_uuid":"d429b585-2cb5-4cd6-9be6-b722131124f0","position":{"commit_sha":"6eea8406e9f422410f0a5e59ee2eca5bbedc2148","position":"1794524328489017001-d429b585-2cb5-4cd6-9be6-b722131124f0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Second independent occurrence — different session, different commit\n\nSame assertion, same line, reached by a different route, which rules out anything specific to\nthe original worktree or commit.\n\n- Session `6a3fecbb-7c5e-4e07-b1ba-7eb2bd09cb7c`, worktree `impl-cb1b`, commit `f2ced750d1b`.\n- `make verify` ran 2 h 18 min (8293.97 s) against a documented 25–30 min, with a second\n  `make verify` running concurrently on the same host, each at `-n 4 --dist worksteal`.\n- `tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py:431: AssertionError`, 0 races in 40\n  rounds.\n- That commit adds MCP async gate tools and touches neither this test nor the code under\n  test.\n\nTwo sightings, two sessions, two unrelated commits, both on a saturated host and both with a\nwall time 5–9× nominal. The common factor is host load, not any change under test.\n\n## Which half of the test fails — worth stating explicitly\n\nThe failure is in the **positive control**, not in the subject. The test is in two parts:\n\n- `:426-431` — up to 40 **uncoordinated** rounds, assert a race was seen at least once.\n- `:433-436` — 8 **coordinated** rounds, assert zero races.\n\nExecution stops at `:431`, so the assertion that actually checks `fetch_coordination_lock`\n(`:436`) is never evaluated. Nothing in either sighting is evidence that the coordination lock\nis broken — a useful thing to have recorded, so a future reader does not re-investigate the\nlock.\n\nThe mechanism is visible in the test's own comment at `:424-425`: \"High base rate → a small\ncap is more than enough; hitting the cap with zero races would itself be astronomically\nunlikely.\" The 6 workers release from a `threading.Barrier(n)` and then each runs a real\n`git fetch`. That base rate is high only while the threads genuinely overlap; on a saturated\nhost they are descheduled after the barrier, the fetches serialize, and the CAS never\ncollides. The base rate is a function of host load, and the test treats it as a constant.\n\n## One acceptance criterion worth adding\n\nThe current ACs are satisfiable by weakening the control until it cannot fail — for example\nby deleting the uncoordinated half outright. That would make the red go away while removing\nthe only thing proving the lock is load-bearing. Suggest adding:\n\n- [ ] The test still FAILS when `fetch_coordination_lock` is disabled or stubbed, demonstrated\n      with a red run. A test that can no longer fail has not been fixed.\n\n## Related but distinct\n\nThe same `make verify` also failed two CLI facade tests on a stale stderr logging handler —\n`cded-334b-a742-4082` (bald-diagnostic-cricket), a confirmed and separate root cause. These\ntwo bugs share only the loaded host, not a mechanism.\n\n`1a3b-e678-0eeb-4230` was filed from this session before this ticket surfaced; it is now\nlinked `duplicates` here and archived.\n","timestamp":1793826493806637344},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 06:00 PST: in_progress. Fix committed in .rebar/worktrees/fix-shark as ec59ea0f0cf, not pushed. The scheduling-dependent positive control is replaced by a deterministic one: a reference-transaction hook (active only in that fetch) moves refs/remotes/origin/tickets in the `preparing` state, so the real fetch fails with \"is at X but expected Y\" and is_ref_cas_mismatch must recognise it; with the hook made a no-op the control fails. The coordination half is its own test (0 mismatches over 8 rounds). Skips on git < 2.48; CI runners have git 2.55/2.56. Passed 5 of 5 at load average 42. Next: make verify, push, close after the Bedrock spend cap releases (16:00 PST).","timestamp":1794491836327784599},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 PST: CLOSED (class preexisting, completion signature signed). Change 3380 merged as e93b4f16396 (PS2 used subprocess_env for the safe-env guard). Plan review and close ran through the worktree CLI on the Anthropic API (anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5) while the Bedrock spend cap held.","timestamp":1794524328489017001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793776063075872001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6f6243f2-0eb7-4d37-9b88-68341bbc5d9e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ad14-c714-4619-4cd2"},{"link_uuid":"50f1387a-87a2-40c8-8075-dab2ed14c8ec","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c387-c5ce-8d1e-4b36"},{"link_uuid":"da8bef3f-47fc-4d89-87ca-2db3f0a29a0d","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"ccd2-528c-b4a9-4b90"}],"description":"## Observation\ntests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py:431 asserted a ref-CAS race in 40 uncoordinated rounds and saw 0 (`AssertionError: expected the uncoordinated parallel fetches to race git's ref CAS`). Observed in make verify on worktree fix-chihuahua at commit 4f8cd749a61 (session a85e3cd3, 2026-11-03/04 PST). The run took 3 h 45 min (documented 25-30 min) while other sessions' review-plan gates ran on the host; the test passed in isolation (`pytest -n0 <nodeid>`) on the same code. The commit does not touch this test or its code under test.\nThe positive control depends on the race actually happening, which host load can prevent, so the test's verdict depends on host scheduling.\n## Testing\n\n`pytest tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py` passes; the forced-race control fails when its hook is made a no-op, and the module passed 5 of 5 runs at load average 42.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Root cause confirmed with a deterministic reproduction (for example the race forced, or the control made independent of scheduling).\n- [x] The test's verdict no longer depends on host load.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py","reason":"deterministic forced CAS race control"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","c387-c5ce-8d1e-4b36"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f01b7fbd-176b-4e1e-b4f3-dc2970dab92f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f121-ed38-6939-43b9","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fetch-race positive control fails when a loaded host serializes the uncoordinated fetches","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d52b7e93-3a6c-47de-a959-eb21cde1e8c2","fc581a1f-5108-4fe8-b02b-410f9ee8927f","064abfad-f862-43ae-95d6-4918cbd37952","76c1f2c7-a3a1-4f9a-a941-aeb36a80737f","2839ea82-c943-4a76-92d6-cd2621093ad3","50f1387a-87a2-40c8-8075-dab2ed14c8ec","87a89e1a-06b9-4111-b55e-f86034d2a6a9","342e16d6-c767-43a6-89d9-a1ed2f791cf8","579b4553-e1f3-45c0-bcff-1f31094fc96f","f01b7fbd-176b-4e1e-b4f3-dc2970dab92f","c806a08b-a56b-450b-89d8-3136ddfb503d","da8bef3f-47fc-4d89-87ca-2db3f0a29a0d","d429b585-2cb5-4cd6-9be6-b722131124f0"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794524328489017002,"uuid":"4821d5f2-29b1-41e7-a615-6a7ad0729abc"}